    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d75">

                <pb facs="0071" n="61" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg61"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lauchlin Currie to President Roosevelt </hi><anchor
                        n="24" xml:id="d75-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-01">June 1, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Re: Attached cable from Madame Chiang Kai-shek.<anchor n="25"
                        xml:id="d75-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>I think the reason behind this request is not so much for consultation as for
                    morale boosting, and as such would be very desirable.</p>
                <p>If Mr. Hopkins goes I do not think my presence would add a lot. On the other
                    hand, if Mr. Hopkins is unable to go I believe I still have a lot of prestige in
                    China as your representative.</p>
                <p>You will note that an immediate reply is requested.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laugh Currie</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
